    ch\xFAng. B\u1ED9 m\xE1y Golgi c\xF3 c\u1EA5u tr\xFAc ph\xE2n c\u1EF1c g\u1ED3m
    m\u1EB7t nh\u1EADp (n\u01A1i ti\u1EBFp nh\u1EADn) v\xE0 m\u1EB7t xu\u1EA5t (n\u01A1i
    xu\u1EA5t \u0111i).</indent>\n\n\u2022<indent=4%><b>Ch\u1EE9c n\u0103ng</b>:
    ti\u1EBFp nh\u1EADn c\xE1c s\u1EA3n ph\u1EA9m t\u1EEB l\u01B0\u1EDBi n\u1ED9i
    ch\u1EA5t; bi\u1EBFn \u0111\u1ED5i, \u0111\xF3ng g\xF3i v\xE0 ph\xE2n ph\u1ED1i
    c\xE1c s\u1EA3n ph\u1EA9m n\xE0y \u0111\u1EBFn c\xE1c v\u1ECB tr\xED kh\xE1c
    nhau. Ngo\xE0i ra, b\u1ED9 m\xE1y Golgi c\xF2n tham gia v\xE0o qu\xE1 tr\xECnh
    t\u1ED5ng h\u1EE3p m\u1ED9t s\u1ED1 polysaccharide v\xE0 ch\u1EA5t n\u1EC1n ngo\u1EA1i
    b\xE0o.</indent>"
